+(duration-opts)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a duration such as `90`, `2d`, or `1h30m` into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. A bare
+number is a count of seconds. Otherwise, the value is one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d`, `h`, `m`,
+and `s`, each at most once and in that order, with no spaces. Units are case-insensitive.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=30m1h'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
